'''Charlie Alexander Villanueva Mejia<ref name="dominican" />''' (born August 24, 1984) is a Dominican-American former professional [[basketball]] player who played for the [[Toronto Raptors]], [[Milwaukee Bucks]], [[Detroit Pistons]] and [[Dallas Mavericks]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA).

The son of immigrants from the Dominican Republic, Villanueva was raised in [[Elmhurst, Queens]], New York City. He was drafted at the age of 20 with the seventh overall pick in the [[2005 NBA draft]] by the [[Toronto Raptors]]. He also holds Dominican citizenship and has represented the [[Dominican Republic men's national basketball team|Dominican Republic national team]] in international competitions.<ref name="dominican">{{cite web|url=http://puertorico2009.fiba.com/pages/eng/fe/09/facm/player/p/eid/4042/pid/49590/sid/4042/tid/274/profile.html|title=Charlie Villanueva Player Profile|access-date=November 27, 2010|publisher=[[FIBA]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100213072221/http://puertorico2009.fiba.com/pages/eng/fe/09/facm/player/p/eid/4042/pid/49590/sid/4042/tid/274/profile.html|archive-date=February 13, 2010|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fiba.com/downloads/Regulations/170310_FIBA_Internal_Regulations.pdf|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101215052416/http://www.fiba.com/downloads/Regulations/170310_FIBA_Internal_Regulations.pdf|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 15, 2010|page=67|title=Internal Regulations 2010|publisher=[[FIBA]]}}</ref>

